dwrite: key cached glyph bitmaps by rendering mode (After Effects crash while scrubbing)

After Effects 2026 crashed 10-30 s into scrubbing a reporter's project (GitHub Neutron#14), always
inside glyph-run rendering (glyphrunanalysis_render, the 1bpp and the 8bpp copy loops) with a wild
destination pointer. The glyph cache keys rendered bitmaps by glyph, size and transform only. An ALIASED
bitmap is 1 bit per pixel and the other modes 8, so a glyph rendered antialiased and later aliased got the
cached 8bpp bitmap copied into a buffer sized for 1bpp: a heap overflow several times the buffer, which
corrupted unrelated memory and crashed later, in varying places. After Effects draws some text aliased and
renders on two threads, so the order and the crash varied from run to run. (Neutron's earlier patch that
put the transform into the key made this reachable at every HiDPI scale; upstream skipped the cache for
any non-identity transform.)

The rendering mode is now part of a bitmap's key, and a cached bitmap whose size differs from the one
requested is rendered again instead of copied.

Harness: preserved-fixes/harnesses/dwrite-mode-cache.c renders one glyph antialiased, then aliased, and
validates the heap: 11.10-110 CORRUPTED, patched valid and the aliased texture equals a fresh render.
After Effects 2026 with the reporter's project (clean room): crashed 2 of 2 runs scrubbing without
logging; patched, 0 of 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Power BI port: Wine 11.18 keeps its transformed-glyph cache bypass; only the bitmap key and size guard are changed. Candidate only, not in the production series. Retains Wine/Neutron LGPL-2.1-or-later terms.

--- a/dlls/dwrite/font.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@
 static HRESULT dwrite_fontface_get_glyph_bitmap(struct dwrite_fontface *fontface, DWRITE_RENDERING_MODE1 rendering_mode,
         unsigned int *is_1bpp, struct dwrite_glyphbitmap *bitmap)
 {
-    struct cache_key key = { .size = bitmap->emsize, .glyph = bitmap->glyph, .mode = DWRITE_MEASURING_MODE_NATURAL };
+    struct cache_key key = { .size = bitmap->emsize, .glyph = bitmap->glyph, .mode = 0x100 | rendering_mode };
     struct get_glyph_bitmap_params params;
     const RECT *bbox = &bitmap->bbox;
     unsigned int bitmap_size, _1bpp;
@@ -225,12 +225,21 @@
     }
     else if ((entry = fontface_get_cache_entry(fontface, bitmap_size, &key)))
     {
-        if (entry->has_bitmap)
+        if (entry->has_bitmap && entry->bitmap_size == bitmap_size)
         {
             memcpy(bitmap->buf, entry->bitmap, entry->bitmap_size);
         }
         else
         {
+            /* Never copy a bitmap sized for a different rendering mode. */
+            if (entry->has_bitmap)
+            {
+                fontface->cache.size -= entry->bitmap_size;
+                fontface->cache.size += bitmap_size;
+                free(entry->bitmap);
+                entry->bitmap = NULL;
+                entry->has_bitmap = 0;
+            }
             params.is_1bpp = &_1bpp;
             UNIX_CALL(get_glyph_bitmap, &params);
 
